  "id": "COMPOUND:781 - DISEASE:2357",
  "verbalization": "Gentamicin is shown to affect osteoglycin, which in turn is implicated in the pathogenesis of Osteogenesis imperfecta, perinatal lethal. This relationship is supported by multiple high-scoring pathways, all of which indicate a direct causal link between Gentamicin and osteoglycin, followed by a downstream effect on the disease. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust mechanistic connection, with osteoglycin acting as a key mediator in the pathophysiology of the condition. The presence of a well-documented mode of action—through its effect on osteoglycin—supports the hypothesis that Gentamicin may have a therapeutic potential in this context. The evidence is grounded in a clear, biologically plausible mechanism, and the shared pathway highlights the importance of osteoglycin in the disease process. The integration of these findings underscores the potential for Gentamicin to be re-evaluated as a treatment for Osteogenesis imperfecta, perinatal lethal, provided further validation of the mechanism is achieved.",
